{"id":536,"root":"ودي","bw":"wdy","tr":"w-d-y","found":true,"html":"<div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">وَدَى القَتِيلَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>He gave the bloodwit to the heir,</em> or <em>next of kin, of the slain person.</em> (Msb.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">وَادَاهُ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> inf. n. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مُوَادَاةٌ</span>, <em>He took</em> [<em>from him</em>] <em>the</em> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">دِيَة</span>. (TA.) See 3 in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عدو</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">أَودَى بِهِ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>It destroyed him;</em> (T;) <em>it removed him,</em> or <em>took him away:</em> (M, K:) said of death [&amp;c.]. (T, M, K.) See an ex. in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">بلو</span>, conj. 8, and another voce <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">أَزْلَمُ</span>. ― -b2- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">أَودَى</span>: see a verse cited voce <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">قَلَبَةٌ</span>. ― -b3- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">أَودَى العَيرُ اِلّا</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">ضَرِطًا</span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">ضَرَطَ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">دِيَةٌ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>Bloodwit; a fine for bloodshed,</em> i. e., <em>homicide;</em> consisting of a hundred camels. ― -b2- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">دِيَاتُ جِرَاحَاتٍ</span> [<em>Fines for wounds</em>]. (S, M, TA, &amp;c., in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">شنق</span>.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">وَدِىٌّ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>Small</em> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">فَسِيل</span>, q. v.; (S, Msb, K;) <em>shoots,</em> or <em>offsets, cut off from palm-trees and planted:</em> (Mgh:) <em>young palm-trees.</em> (TA.) </div>","pages":null,"shownPages":null,"chars":1586,"entries":5,"shownEntries":5,"truncated":false,"match":"direct","key":"wdy"}